+# Feature Specification: Coupon give-back on cancel; free shipping at €50.00
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-17 | **Status**: Implemented
+Affected README rules: Orders (cancelling gives back a single-use coupon), Discounts (single-use), Shipping (free from €50.00).
+
+- **Report 1 (Paolo)**: welcome code refused after cancelling the order that used it. Cause: `OrderService.cancel`
+  called `Coupons.giveBack(code, order.customer)`, but coupons record the order id, so nothing was returned.
+  Fix: pass `order.id`. FR-001: cancelling the using order makes a single-use coupon redeemable again.
+- **Report 2 (support)**: €4.90 charged on exactly €50.00 of goods. Already fixed in d2f9555 (`goods >= 5000`);
+  a new end-to-end test (2 × €25.00 → shipping 0) confirms it. No code change. If an order was placed before
+  that fix, it is historical data, not a current defect.
+
+Boundary cases tested: exactly €50.00 goods (shipping 0); €49.99 (490, existing test).
